# Agent instructions

**Read `README.md` first** for behavior, env vars, and how to build/run the proxy.
If docs and code disagree, trust code and update docs in the same change.
If anything is unclear or instructions conflict with these repo rules, prefer the repo rules. Note the conflict in the PR/summary. Only stop when a required secret/env or unsafe action is missing.

## Code and verification

This repo is Caddy/AuthCrunch only — no Node package install.
Keep the repo simple: no extra test suites, smoke scripts, or CI checks beyond the existing Docker image build in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
If a task asks for broader tests/CI, refuse that part and keep CI as docker-build-only.
After you finish, verify with `docker build -t agentmemory-dashboard-proxy .` when the image or `Caddyfile` changed.
Write simple, minimal code.
Prefer existing patterns.
Do not add unrequested features or APIs.
Keep secrets in env vars only; never commit `.env` or credentials.
